WHICH ESTIMATOR PRODUCED `.ENT_SO_PCO2_AMP` = 19.45 ? 
  (1) harmonic of the AREA-MEAN series    16.26 uatm   <- GATE S's phase uses this 
  (2) AREA-MEAN of PER-CELL amplitudes    19.68 uatm   <- PHASE-BLIND 
  the constant is closest to (2). 
⛔ ⇒ THE PROJECT'S AMPLITUDE CONSTANT AND ITS PHASE CONSTANT COME FROM TWO 
   DIFFERENT CONVENTIONS ON THE SAME PRODUCT AND BAND -- [[amp_definition_mismatch]]. 
⭐ AND THE PHYSICS PICKS ONE: `ent_seas_amp_SH` perturbs a SINGLE WELL-MIXED BOX, 
   whose concentration is the AREA MEAN. For a box, the area mean of the anomaly IS 
   the anomaly of the area mean, so (1) is correct and (2) overstates it: (2) averages 
   |amplitude| and so discards the phase cancellation a box cannot avoid. 
⚠ BUT DO NOT CORRECT ONE LEG OF A TWO-LEG SUM ALONE. The prior centre adds a 
   SOLUBILITY term (46.95 uatm, from .ENT_SO_SST_AMP = 3.0 K) to this one, and that 
   term's own convention -- per-cell or area-mean -- IS NOT STATED in constants.R. 
   If it is also per-cell, the two biases partially CANCEL in the sum. Establish the 
   SST leg's convention before changing either. 
⇒ IMPACT IS SMALL EITHER WAY: swapping 19.45 -> 16.26 moves the in-band value 
   29.68 -> 28.25 and the prior centre 10.95 -> 10.43, a 4.8 % change, because the 
   SOLUBILITY term dominates the sum. A real defect, a modest number. 
 
⚠ RULINGS OWED BEFORE THIS BECOMES A GATE: 
  1. WHICH BAND maps to the model's SH mixed layer? The model's `ml` is the 
     LOW-LATITUDE surface box (hs_frac splits the high latitudes into `hs`), 
     so this is a real choice -- and it is the choice that BIT GATE S, whose 
     SH-area-mean bracket EXCLUDED the right answer while CONTAINING the 
     pre-fix model. Reuse GATE S's settled convention; do not invent a second. 
  2. THE MODEL SIDE DOES NOT EXIST YET: ccx_run()$out carries ml_C and ml_C13 
     but NO mixed-layer pCO2, and neither does the flux trace. That output 
     must be added before any comparison can be made. 
⛔ pCO2 IS NOT FLUX. These are pCO2 amplitudes and may not be quoted as flux 
   amplitudes: F = k*K0*dpCO2 and neither the wind seasonality in k nor the 
   temperature seasonality in K0 is present here. 
 
